From 69349e9415e2b0ec136ae4e801eb851ccc43d71f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mertcanekiz <ekiz.mertcan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 23:37:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: DP-IN v5: Thunderbolt DP tunnel driven hotplug and
 forced modeset on reconnect

- thunderbolt: tb_dp_tunnel_notifier_register/unregister with TB_DP_TUNNEL_UP/DOWN
  events for tunnels starting at a host router DP IN adapter (activation in
  tb_tunnel_one_dp, teardown in tb_deactivate_and_free_tunnel). Active tunnels
  are replayed to late subscribers.
- appledrm: subscribe when routed into a DP IN adapter (DT apple,tbt-nhi selects
  the host interface); a retrying work item runs dcp_dptx_connect_oob /
  dcp_dptx_disconnect_oob so the LG comes up at boot and after any link drop
  without the debugfs trigger (appledrm.dpin_auto=0 disables it).
- appledrm: after a tunnel reconnect the compositor keeps its output state and
  never re-sends the mode (firmware "swallows" swaps with the pipeline powered
  down). dcp_crtc_atomic_check now forces a modeset when the mode is invalid,
  and apple_crtc_atomic_enable powers the DCP back on when the firmware
  pipeline was powered down by HPD removal (dcp->powered).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
